    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22776" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραμμ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>linear, geometrical</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					<u>UP</u>
					10.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόδειξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Marc.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάγκαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Olymp.
					<u>in Grg.</u>
					p.260
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<i>by means of lines, geometrically</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδείκνυσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					3.92
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Alm.</u>
				2.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
			</span></i><i>in R.</i><i><span class="en">
				2.27
			</span></i> K. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. ἀριθμός</span>
